Q: Dynamic checkbox HTML generated by CodeIgniter model method only returns last iterations after looping A: <p>It is overwriting:</p>

<pre><code>$str = $b.$a;
</code></pre>

<p>This string changes every loop again. If you want to make it an array, do this</p>

<pre><code>$str[] = $b.$a;
</code></pre>

<p>If you want to add it to the text:</p>

<pre><code>$str .= $b.$a;
</code></pre>

Q: Using POST in Rest API just like get to add 2 numbers A: <p>I am assuming that you are calling this url from a browser and a browser is always going to do a GET on the url. If you want to try POST, you will have to either write a REST client in any one of your preferred languages (javascript, java) or if you are using firefox you can use POSTER plugin to simulate a POST. See here: <a href="https://addons.mozilla.org/en-US/firefox/addon/poster/" rel="nofollow">POSTER</a>. </p>

<p>Here is a quick REST client example (code snippet) in java. I have used jersey REST client.</p>

<pre><code>WebResource webResource = restClient.resource("/calcrest/calc/add");
webResource = webResource.path("1").path("5");

String response = webResource.type(MediaType.TEXT_PLAIN)
                .accept(MediaType.TEXT_PLAIN)
                .post(ClientResponse.class);
System.out.println("Your addition: "+response);
</code></pre>

<p>I hope this helps!</p>
